module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.ConormalClassLocal
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.PolynomialPresheafSections
public import StacksFrontier.Cotangent.SheavesOfRings.NaiveComparisonArrow
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.ConormalIdealRestriction
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.FreeAlgebraBaseChangeSurjective
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.FreeAlgebraConormalBaseChange

/-!
# Surjectivity and kernel of the conormal map of a base change of presentations

Let `u : 𝒜₁ ⟶ 𝒜₂` be a morphism of sheaves of commutative rings on a site, let `ℰ` be a
presheaf of sets and let `e : ℰ ⟶ ℬ` be a family of generators of a sheaf of rings `ℬ` over
`𝒜₂`. `StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.FreeAlgebraConormalBaseChange` compares the two
polynomial presentations `𝒜₁[ℰ] ↠ ℬ` and `𝒜₂[ℰ] ↠ ℬ` of that family and builds the induced map
`ℐ'/(ℐ')² ⟶ ℐ/ℐ²` of conormal sheaves. This file proves that that map is **surjective**, i.e.
locally surjective, i.e. an epimorphism, as soon as `u` is, identifies its kernel with
`𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]`, where `𝒥 = Ker u`, and **performs the descent**: a homomorphism `ℐ'/(ℐ')² ⟶ 𝒢` which
kills the conormal classes of the generators of `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]` factors through `ℐ/ℐ²`, in exactly
one way.

This is the descent that Step 1 of the proof of [Stacks 08U8] performs on the difference of the
two restrictions `b|_{ℐ'}` and `ν ∘ a|_{ℐ'}`; the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.ConormalIdealRestriction` record it as missing.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sites.FreeAlgebra.isLocallySurjective_freeAlgebraSheafDesc`: a presentation
  `𝒜[ℰ] ⟶ ℬ` is locally surjective as soon as its family of generators `ℰ ⟶ ℬ` is. This
  discharges the standing hypothesis on a family of generators of [Stacks 08TL] from the
  property the applications actually establish.
* `Stacks.Sites.FreeAlgebra.ker_mvPolynomialMap`: the kernel of `MvPolynomial.map f` is the
  ideal generated by the constants in `Ker f`, for an arbitrary ring map `f`.
* `Stacks.Sites.FreeAlgebra.coefficientKernelSieve_mem`: **the kernel of base change is locally
  generated by `Ker u`** — a local section of `𝒜₁[ℰ]` killed by `𝒜₁[ℰ] ⟶ 𝒜₂[ℰ]` lies, locally
  on the site, in the ideal `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]` generated by the coefficients in `𝒥 = Ker u`.
* `Stacks.Sites.Conormal.isLocallySurjective_presentationConormalMap` and
  `Stacks.Sites.Conormal.epi_presentationConormalMap`: the conormal map `ℐ'/(ℐ')² ⟶ ℐ/ℐ²` is
  locally surjective, i.e. surjective as a map of sheaves of `ℬ`-modules, i.e. an epimorphism.
* `Stacks.Sites.Conormal.presentationConormalMap_conormalClass_coefficient_mul`: the conormal
  map kills the conormal class of a local section of `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]`. With the previous item this is
  the inclusion `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ] ⊆ Ker(ℐ' ⟶ ℐ)` reverse to it.
* `Stacks.Sites.Conormal.descend_unique`: a homomorphism out of `ℐ'/(ℐ')²` descends along the
  conormal map in at most one way.
* `Stacks.Sites.Conormal.existsUnique_descend`: **the descent criterion**, for an arbitrary
  epimorphism of sheaves of modules — a homomorphism out of its source which kills every local
  section the epimorphism kills factors through it, in exactly one way.
* `Stacks.Sites.Conormal.eq_zero_of_presentationConormalMap_eq_zero`: **the kernel
  computation** — a local section of `ℐ'/(ℐ')²` killed by the conormal map is killed by every
  homomorphism killing the conormal classes of the generators of `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]`.
* `Stacks.Sites.Conormal.existsUnique_descend_presentationConormalMap`: **the descent of Step 1
  of the proof of [Stacks 08U8]** — such a homomorphism `ℐ'/(ℐ')² ⟶ 𝒢` factors through
  `ℐ/ℐ² ⟶ 𝒢` in exactly one way.
* `Stacks.Sites.Conormal.existsUnique_descend_conormalDifference`: the same for the difference
  cocycle of two restriction data which agree on `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]`, which is the form Step 1 of the
  source's proof uses it in. This is the statement whose absence the implementation notes of
  `StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.ConormalIdealRestriction` record.

## Implementation notes

The objectwise map of polynomial rings is `MvPolynomial.map` of `u` on sections. Local
surjectivity of it is proved by induction on a polynomial: the constants are locally in the
image because `u` is locally surjective, the variables are globally in the image, and the set
of polynomials that are locally in the image is closed under addition and under multiplication
by a variable because a Grothendieck topology is closed under intersection of covering sieves.

Local surjectivity transfers to the sheaves `𝒜ᵢ[ℰ]` because the sheafification unit is locally
bijective, which is the hypothesis `J.WEqualsLocallyBijective CommRingCat` carried here: the
unit is then locally surjective, so the composite `𝒜₁(-)[ℰ(-)] ⟶ 𝒜₂(-)[ℰ(-)] ⟶ 𝒜₂[ℰ]` is, and
`Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_isLocallySurjective_fac` reads off the base change morphism
from the factorisation of that composite through the unit of `𝒜₁[ℰ]`.

For the conormal map the same pattern is used one level up: the sheafification unit of the
conormal presheaf is locally surjective, so by transitivity of the topology it suffices to
treat a local section of the shape `conormalClass g` with `g` a local section of `ℐ`, and there
`g` lifts locally along the base change morphism — a lift automatically lies in `ℐ'` because
`ℐ'` is the preimage of `ℐ`. No local section of `ℐ/ℐ²` is ever lifted globally; the two
covering sieves are composed with `GrothendieckTopology.transitive`.

The kernel computation runs the same way in reverse: a local section of `𝒜₁[ℰ]` killed by base
change comes locally from a polynomial, whose image under `MvPolynomial.map u` is then locally
zero because the sheafification unit is locally *injective*, and a polynomial killed by
`MvPolynomial.map u` lies in the ideal generated by the constants in `Ker u`. The last step is
`ker_mvPolynomialMap`, pure commutative algebra and the only place where the polynomials are
taken apart coefficient by coefficient.

The descent itself is split in two. The categorical half is
`Stacks.Sites.Conormal.existsUnique_descend`: an epimorphism in an abelian category is the
cokernel of its kernel, and the sections of the kernel of a morphism of sheaves of modules are
the local sections it kills, so `CategoryTheory.Abelian.epiDesc` applies as soon as the
homomorphism kills those. The concrete half, `eq_zero_of_presentationConormalMap_eq_zero`,
verifies that hypothesis, and is where the work is: a local section of `ℐ'/(ℐ')²` killed by the
conormal map comes, on a covering sieve, from a local section `c` of `ℐ'`; the conormal class of
`β c` then vanishes in `ℐ/ℐ²`, so `β c` lies *locally* in `ℐ²`, since the module sheafification
unit is locally injective and `Ideal.toCotangent_eq_zero` identifies its objectwise kernel; a
product decomposition of `ℐ²` lifts factor by factor to `(ℐ')²` along the base change morphism,
and the lifted product has conormal class zero; and the leftover difference is killed by base
change, so `coefficientKernelSieve_mem` puts it locally in `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]`, where
`eq_zero_of_mem_coefficientKernelIdeal` applies.

Vanishing of a local section of `𝒢` is tracked by `Stacks.Sites.Conormal.moduleVanishingSieve`, the
sieve on which it restricts to zero.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08U8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08U8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08UC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08UC)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe v u w z t t'

namespace Stacks.Sites.FreeAlgebra

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)

/-- **The kernel of `MvPolynomial.map f`** is the ideal generated by the constants in the kernel
of `f`: a polynomial is killed exactly when each of its coefficients is, and it is then the sum
of its monomials `C a * X^s` with `a ∈ Ker f`. No surjectivity of `f` is needed. -/
theorem ker_mvPolynomialMap {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (f : R →+* S)
    (σ : Type*) :
    RingHom.ker (MvPolynomial.map (σ := σ) f) =
      Ideal.span (MvPolynomial.C '' (RingHom.ker f : Set R)) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun p hp ↦ ?_) ?_
  · have hcoeff : ∀ s : σ →₀ ℕ, f (MvPolynomial.coeff s p) = 0 := by
      intro s
      rw [← MvPolynomial.coeff_map, show MvPolynomial.map f p = 0 from hp,
        MvPolynomial.coeff_zero]
    rw [p.as_sum]
    refine Ideal.sum_mem _ fun s _ ↦ ?_
    rw [MvPolynomial.monomial_eq]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _
      (Ideal.subset_span ⟨_, RingHom.mem_ker.mpr (hcoeff s), rfl⟩)
  · rw [Ideal.span_le]
    rintro x ⟨r, hr, rfl⟩
    show MvPolynomial.map f (MvPolynomial.C r) = 0
    rw [MvPolynomial.map_C, show f r = 0 from RingHom.mem_ker.mp hr, map_zero]

variable [HasWeakSheafify J CommRingCat.{w}]

/-- Objectwise evaluation of `𝒜₁(-)[ℰ(-)]` in `𝒜₂[ℰ]` along the base change data is the
objectwise map of polynomial rings followed by the sheafification unit of `𝒜₂(-)[ℰ(-)]`. -/
lemma polynomialEvaluation_eq_polynomialBaseChange_comp
    {A₁ A₂ : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}} (u : A₁ ⟶ A₂) (E : Functor Cᵒᵖ (Type w)) :
    polynomialEvaluation J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) E
        (u ≫ freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₂ E) (freeAlgebraSheafVariable J A₂ E) =
      polynomialBaseChange J u E ≫
        CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (polynomialPresheaf J A₂ E) := by
  apply NatTrans.ext
  funext U
  apply CommRingCat.hom_ext
  apply MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext
  · intro r
    refine (MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_C _ _ _).trans ?_
    exact congrArg ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (polynomialPresheaf J A₂ E)).app U).hom
      (MvPolynomial.map_C _ _).symm
  · intro x
    refine (MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_X' _ _ _).trans ?_
    exact congrArg ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (polynomialPresheaf J A₂ E)).app U).hom
      (MvPolynomial.map_X _ _).symm

/-- **A presentation is surjective as soon as its family of generators is.** If the family
`e : ℰ ⟶ ℬ` is locally surjective as a morphism of presheaves of sets then the induced
`𝒜[ℰ] ⟶ ℬ` is locally surjective, because a local section of `ℬ` that is `e(x)` is the value of
the variable `X x`.

This is the source's standing hypothesis on a family of generators ([Stacks 08TL]) derived from
the only thing one ever knows about `ℰ` in the applications, namely that its sections generate
`ℬ` locally; `Stacks.Sites.FreeAlgebra.canonicalPresentation_isLocallySurjective` is the special
case `ℰ = ℬ`. -/
theorem isLocallySurjective_freeAlgebraSheafDesc (A B : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w})
    (E : Functor Cᵒᵖ (Type w)) (a : A ⟶ B) (e : E ⟶ underlyingPresheaf J B)
    [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J e] :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (freeAlgebraSheafDesc J A B E a e).hom := by
  have h : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (polynomialEvaluation J A B E a e) := by
    constructor
    intro U b
    refine J.superset_covering ?_ (Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J e b)
    rintro V i ⟨x, hx⟩
    exact ⟨MvPolynomial.X x, (MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_X' _ _ _).trans hx⟩
  exact Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_isLocallySurjective_fac J
    (freeAlgebraSheafDesc_spec J A B E a e)

variable [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective CommRingCat.{w}]

/-! ### The kernel of base change -/

omit [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective CommRingCat.{w}] in
/-- The structural morphism `𝒜 ⟶ 𝒜[ℰ]` is, on presheaves, the coefficient inclusion followed by
the sheafification unit. -/
lemma freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap_hom (A : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w})
    (E : Functor Cᵒᵖ (Type w)) :
    (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A E).hom =
      polynomialCoefficientMap J A E ≫
        CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (polynomialPresheaf J A E) :=
  rfl

omit [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective CommRingCat.{w}] in
/-- On sections, the structural morphism `𝒜 ⟶ 𝒜[ℰ]` is the class of a constant polynomial. -/
lemma freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap_app_apply (A : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w})
    (E : Functor Cᵒᵖ (Type w)) (X : Cᵒᵖ) (r : A.obj.obj X) :
    (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A E).hom.app X r =
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (polynomialPresheaf J A E)).app X (MvPolynomial.C r) :=
  rfl

/-- The ideal `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]` of Step 1 of the proof of [Stacks 08U8], where `𝒥 = Ker u`: the ideal
of `𝒜₁[ℰ](U)` generated by the coefficients belonging to the kernel of `u`. -/
noncomputable def coefficientKernelIdeal {A₁ A₂ : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}} (u : A₁ ⟶ A₂)
    (E : Functor Cᵒᵖ (Type w)) (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Ideal ((freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj X) :=
  Ideal.span (((freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E).hom.app X).hom ''
    (RingHom.ker (u.hom.app X).hom : Set (A₁.obj.obj X)))

omit [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective CommRingCat.{w}] in
/-- The restriction maps carry `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]` into itself. -/
lemma coefficientKernelIdeal_le_comap {A₁ A₂ : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}} (u : A₁ ⟶ A₂)
    (E : Functor Cᵒᵖ (Type w)) {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    coefficientKernelIdeal J u E X ≤
      (coefficientKernelIdeal J u E Y).comap ((freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map f).hom := by
  rw [coefficientKernelIdeal, Ideal.span_le]
  rintro x ⟨j, hj, rfl⟩
  have hmem : (A₁.obj.map f) j ∈ RingHom.ker (u.hom.app Y).hom := by
    refine RingHom.mem_ker.mpr ?_
    rw [NatTrans.naturality_apply, show (u.hom.app X) j = 0 from RingHom.mem_ker.mp hj,
      map_zero]
  refine Ideal.mem_comap.mpr ?_
  rw [← NatTrans.naturality_apply (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E).hom f j]
  exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨_, hmem, rfl⟩

/-- The sieve on which a local section of `𝒜₁[ℰ]` lies in the ideal `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]`. -/
def coefficientKernelSieve {A₁ A₂ : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}} (u : A₁ ⟶ A₂)
    (E : Functor Cᵒᵖ (Type w)) (X : C) (h : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj (op X)) :
    Sieve X where
  arrows V i :=
    (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map i.op h ∈ coefficientKernelIdeal J u E (op V)
  downward_closed := by
    intro V W i hi j
    have hcomp : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map (j ≫ i).op h =
        ((freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map j.op)
          ((freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map i.op h) :=
      congrArg (fun k : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj (op X) ⟶
          (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj (op W) ↦ k.hom h)
        ((freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map_comp i.op j.op)
    change _ ∈ coefficientKernelIdeal J u E (op W)
    rw [hcomp]
    exact coefficientKernelIdeal_le_comap J u E j.op hi

/-- **The kernel of base change is locally generated by the kernel of `u`.** A local section of
`𝒜₁[ℰ]` killed by the base change morphism `𝒜₁[ℰ] ⟶ 𝒜₂[ℰ]` lies, locally on the site, in the
ideal `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]` generated by the coefficients in `𝒥 = Ker u`.

Together with `Stacks.Sites.Conormal.presentationConormalMap_conormalClass_coefficient_mul`,
which is the reverse inclusion, this is the identification of the kernel of `ℐ' ⟶ ℐ` with
`𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]` that Step 1 of the proof of [Stacks 08U8] uses. -/
theorem coefficientKernelSieve_mem {A₁ A₂ : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}} (u : A₁ ⟶ A₂)
    (E : Functor Cᵒᵖ (Type w)) (X : C) (h : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj (op X))
    (hh : (baseChange J u E).hom.app (op X) h = 0) :
    coefficientKernelSieve J u E X h ∈ J X := by
  have hsurj₁ : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (polynomialPresheaf J A₁ E)) :=
    (GrothendieckTopology.W_toSheafify J _).isLocallySurjective
  have hinj₂ : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (polynomialPresheaf J A₂ E)) :=
    (GrothendieckTopology.W_toSheafify J _).isLocallyInjective
  have fac : CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (polynomialPresheaf J A₁ E) ≫
      (baseChange J u E).hom =
        polynomialBaseChange J u E ≫
          CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (polynomialPresheaf J A₂ E) :=
    (freeAlgebraSheafDesc_spec J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) E
      (u ≫ freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₂ E) (freeAlgebraSheafVariable J A₂ E)).trans
      (polynomialEvaluation_eq_polynomialBaseChange_comp J u E)
  refine J.transitive (hsurj₁.imageSieve_mem h) _ ?_
  intro V i hi
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := hi
  have hnat := NatTrans.naturality_apply (baseChange J u E).hom i.op h
  rw [hh, map_zero] at hnat
  have h0 : (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (polynomialPresheaf J A₂ E)).app (op V)
      ((polynomialBaseChange J u E).app (op V) p) = 0 :=
    (congrArg (fun k : polynomialPresheaf J A₁ E ⟶ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E).obj ↦
        (k.app (op V)).hom p) fac).symm.trans
      ((congrArg ((baseChange J u E).hom.app (op V)) hp).trans hnat)
  refine J.superset_covering ?_ (hinj₂.equalizerSieve_mem
    ((polynomialBaseChange J u E).app (op V) p) 0 (by rw [h0, map_zero]))
  intro W j hj
  have hjz : (polynomialPresheaf J A₂ E).map j.op
      ((polynomialBaseChange J u E).app (op V) p) = 0 := by
    rw [hj, map_zero]
  have hker : (polynomialPresheaf J A₁ E).map j.op p ∈
      Ideal.span (MvPolynomial.C '' (RingHom.ker (u.hom.app (op W)).hom :
        Set (A₁.obj.obj (op W)))) := by
    rw [← ker_mvPolynomialMap]
    exact RingHom.mem_ker.mpr
      ((NatTrans.naturality_apply (polynomialBaseChange J u E) j.op p).trans hjz)
  have hle : ∀ q : (polynomialPresheaf J A₁ E).obj (op W),
      q ∈ Ideal.span (MvPolynomial.C '' (RingHom.ker (u.hom.app (op W)).hom :
        Set (A₁.obj.obj (op W)))) →
      q ∈ (coefficientKernelIdeal J u E (op W)).comap
        ((CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (polynomialPresheaf J A₁ E)).app (op W)).hom := by
    intro q hq
    induction hq using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨r, hr, rfl⟩ := hx
      exact Ideal.mem_comap.mpr (Ideal.subset_span
        ⟨r, hr, (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap_app_apply J A₁ E (op W) r).symm⟩)
    | zero => exact Submodule.zero_mem _
    | add x y _ _ hx hy => exact Ideal.add_mem _ hx hy
    | smul a x _ hx => exact Submodule.smul_mem _ a hx
  have hmap : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map (j ≫ i).op h =
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (polynomialPresheaf J A₁ E)).app (op W)
        ((polynomialPresheaf J A₁ E).map j.op p) :=
    ((congrArg (fun k : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj (op X) ⟶
          (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj (op W) ↦ k.hom h)
        ((freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map_comp i.op j.op)).trans
      (congrArg ((freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map j.op) hp.symm)).trans
      (NatTrans.naturality_apply
        (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (polynomialPresheaf J A₁ E)) j.op p).symm
  show (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map (j ≫ i).op h ∈
    coefficientKernelIdeal J u E (op W)
  rw [hmap]
  exact Ideal.mem_comap.mp (hle _ hker)

end Stacks.Sites.FreeAlgebra

namespace Stacks.Sites.Conormal

/-! ### Descent of a homomorphism along an epimorphism of sheaves of modules

The descent criterion in the form in which the conormal map below consumes it: an epimorphism of
sheaves of modules is the cokernel of its kernel, and the sections of its kernel are exactly the
local sections it kills, so a homomorphism out of its source descends as soon as it kills every
local section the epimorphism kills. -/

section EpiDescent

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  {Rg : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}} [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  {M₁ M₂ G : SheafOfModules.{max w u v z} Rg} (p : M₁ ⟶ M₂) (ξ : M₁ ⟶ G)

omit [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}] in
/-- A homomorphism of sheaves of modules which kills every local section killed by `p` is killed
by the kernel inclusion of `p`: a local section of `kernel p` is killed by `p`, since
`kernel.ι p ≫ p = 0`. -/
lemma kernel_ι_comp_eq_zero
    (hξ : ∀ (X : Cᵒᵖ) (x : M₁.val.obj X), p.val.app X x = 0 → ξ.val.app X x = 0) :
    CategoryTheory.Limits.kernel.ι p ≫ ξ = 0 := by
  apply SheafOfModules.hom_ext
  apply PresheafOfModules.hom_ext
  intro X
  apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
  apply LinearMap.ext
  intro y
  refine hξ X ((CategoryTheory.Limits.kernel.ι p).val.app X y) ?_
  exact congrArg
    (fun k : CategoryTheory.Limits.kernel p ⟶ M₂ ↦ (k.val.app X) y)
    (CategoryTheory.Limits.kernel.condition p)

/-- **The existence half of the descent along an epimorphism of sheaves of modules.** A
homomorphism out of the source of an epimorphism `p` which kills every local section killed by
`p` factors through `p`, in exactly one way. The factorization exists because an epimorphism in
an abelian category is the cokernel of its kernel, and is unique because `p` is an
epimorphism. -/
theorem existsUnique_descend [Epi p]
    (hξ : ∀ (X : Cᵒᵖ) (x : M₁.val.obj X), p.val.app X x = 0 → ξ.val.app X x = 0) :
    ∃! ψ : M₂ ⟶ G, p ≫ ψ = ξ := by
  have hk := kernel_ι_comp_eq_zero p ξ hξ
  exact ⟨Abelian.epiDesc p ξ hk, Abelian.comp_epiDesc p ξ hk,
    fun ψ hψ ↦ (cancel_epi p).mp (hψ.trans (Abelian.comp_epiDesc p ξ hk).symm)⟩

end EpiDescent

/-! ### Local vanishing of a section of a sheaf of modules

The descent below proves the vanishing of a section of `𝒢` by refining a covering sieve six
times, so the bookkeeping is factored out: a section is *locally zero* when the sieve on which
it restricts to zero — a sieve, because the restriction maps are additive — is covering, and
that property is closed under addition, is inherited from a covering family of restrictions, and
implies vanishing because `𝒢` is a sheaf. -/

section LocallyZero

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {Rg : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}
  (G : SheafOfModules.{max w u v z} Rg)

/-- The sieve on which a local section of a sheaf of modules restricts to zero, read on the
underlying presheaf of abelian groups so that restriction does not change the type. -/
def moduleVanishingSieve {Y : C} (t : G.val.presheaf.obj (op Y)) : Sieve Y where
  arrows V i := G.val.presheaf.map i.op t = 0
  downward_closed := by
    intro V W i hi j
    show G.val.presheaf.map (j ≫ i).op t = 0
    rw [show ((j ≫ i).op : op Y ⟶ op W) = i.op ≫ j.op from rfl, G.val.presheaf.map_comp]
    change G.val.presheaf.map j.op (G.val.presheaf.map i.op t) = 0
    rw [show G.val.presheaf.map i.op t = 0 from hi, map_zero]

variable {G}

/-- The zero section restricts to zero on the maximal sieve. -/
lemma moduleVanishingSieve_zero_mem {Y : C} :
    moduleVanishingSieve G (0 : G.val.presheaf.obj (op Y)) ∈ J Y :=
  J.superset_covering (fun _ i _ ↦ show G.val.presheaf.map i.op 0 = 0 from map_zero _)
    (J.top_mem Y)

/-- A sum of two sections restricting to zero on covering sieves restricts to zero on a covering
sieve. -/
lemma moduleVanishingSieve_add_mem {Y : C} {t t' : G.val.presheaf.obj (op Y)}
    (h : moduleVanishingSieve G t ∈ J Y) (h' : moduleVanishingSieve G t' ∈ J Y) :
    moduleVanishingSieve G (t + t') ∈ J Y := by
  refine J.superset_covering ?_ (J.intersection_covering h h')
  rintro V i ⟨hi, hi'⟩
  show G.val.presheaf.map i.op (t + t') = 0
  rw [map_add, show G.val.presheaf.map i.op t = 0 from hi,
    show G.val.presheaf.map i.op t' = 0 from hi', add_zero]

/-- A section each of whose restrictions along a covering sieve restricts to zero on a covering
sieve itself restricts to zero on a covering sieve. -/
lemma moduleVanishingSieve_mem_of_restrict {Y : C} (t : G.val.presheaf.obj (op Y))
    (S : Sieve Y) (hS : S ∈ J Y)
    (h : ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (i : V ⟶ Y), S.arrows i →
      moduleVanishingSieve G (G.val.presheaf.map i.op t) ∈ J V) :
    moduleVanishingSieve G t ∈ J Y := by
  refine J.transitive hS _ (fun V i hi ↦ J.superset_covering ?_ (h i hi))
  intro W j hj
  show G.val.presheaf.map (j ≫ i).op t = 0
  rw [show ((j ≫ i).op : op Y ⟶ op W) = i.op ≫ j.op from rfl, G.val.presheaf.map_comp]
  exact hj

/-- **A section of a sheaf of modules restricting to zero on a covering sieve is zero.** -/
lemma eq_zero_of_moduleVanishingSieve_mem [J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z})]
    {Y : C} (t : G.val.presheaf.obj (op Y)) (h : moduleVanishingSieve G t ∈ J Y) : t = 0 := by
  have hsep : Presieve.IsSeparated J (G.val.presheaf ⋙ forget AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}) := by
    apply Presieve.IsSheaf.isSeparated
    rw [← CategoryTheory.isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type]
    exact ((sheafCompose J (forget AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z})).obj
      (⟨G.val.presheaf, G.isSheaf⟩ : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z})).2
  refine (hsep _ h).ext (fun V i hi ↦ ?_)
  show G.val.presheaf.map i.op t = G.val.presheaf.map i.op 0
  rw [show G.val.presheaf.map i.op t = 0 from hi, map_zero]

end LocallyZero

end Stacks.Sites.Conormal

namespace Stacks.Sites.Conormal

open Stacks.Sites.FreeAlgebra

/-! ### Algebraic rules for the conormal class of a local section

The conormal class of a local section of the kernel ideal of a presentation is additive in that
section, semilinear over the presentation, and compatible with the restriction maps. These three
rules, together with the vanishing of the class of a section of the square of the ideal, are what
the descent of a homomorphism out of `ℐ'/(ℐ')²` is computed with below. -/

section ConormalClassAlgebra

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]

/-- The restriction maps of the conormal presheaf send the conormal class of a local section of
the kernel ideal to the conormal class of its restriction. -/
lemma conormalPresheaf_map_toCotangent {A' B' : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{t}} (φ : A' ⟶ B')
    {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (x : kernelIdeal φ X) :
    (conormalPresheaf φ).map f ((kernelIdeal φ X).toCotangent x) =
      (kernelIdeal φ Y).toCotangent ⟨(A'.map f).hom x, map_kernel φ f x.2⟩ :=
  rfl

variable (R A B : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}) (a : R ⟶ A) (φ : A ⟶ B)
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J φ.hom]

omit [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}] in
/-- The conormal class of a local section of the kernel ideal whose value is zero is zero. -/
lemma conormalClass_eq_zero (X : Cᵒᵖ) (y : kernelIdeal φ.hom X) (hy : y.1 = 0) :
    conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J R A B a φ X y = 0 := by
  obtain rfl : y = 0 := Subtype.ext hy
  exact conormalClass_zero J R A B a φ X

omit [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}] in
/-- **The conormal class is semilinear over the presentation.** Scaling a local section of the
kernel ideal by a local section `r` of the source scales its conormal class by the image of `r`
in the target, written here through the image presheaf of the presentation so that the scalar is
literally a section of the sheaf of rings the conormal sheaf is a module over.

Not the same statement as `Stacks.Sites.Conormal.conormalClass_smul`, at
`StacksFrontier/Cotangent/SheavesOfRings/NaiveComparisonArrow.lean:134`, which scales by
`(φ.hom.app X).hom r`, a section of the *sheafified* target `ℬ`.  Here the scalar is
`(quotientToRingSheaf J A B φ).app X (Ideal.Quotient.mk (kernelIdeal φ.hom X) r)`, a section of
the image presheaf `𝒜/ℐ`; that is the scalar the descent below has to hand, and the two live in
different modules structures on the conormal sheaf, so neither statement is an instance of the
other. -/
lemma conormalClass_smul_quotientToRingSheaf (X : Cᵒᵖ) (r : A.obj.obj X)
    (x : kernelIdeal φ.hom X) :
    conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J R A B a φ X (r • x) =
      (quotientToRingSheaf J A B φ).app X (Ideal.Quotient.mk (kernelIdeal φ.hom X) r) •
        conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J R A B a φ X x := by
  have h1 : (kernelIdeal φ.hom X).toCotangent (r • x) =
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (kernelIdeal φ.hom X) r) • (kernelIdeal φ.hom X).toCotangent x :=
    map_smul (kernelIdeal φ.hom X).toCotangent r x
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (toAssociatedModule.{v, u, w, z} J A B φ (conormalPresheaf φ.hom) X)
    h1) ?_
  exact toAssociatedModule_smul.{v, u, w, z} J A B φ (conormalPresheaf φ.hom) X _ _

omit [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}] in
/-- **The conormal class commutes with the restriction maps**, stated at the canonical
restriction of the section.

The pre-existing `Stacks.Sites.Conormal.conormalClass_map`, at
`StacksFrontier/Cotangent/SheavesOfRings/NaiveComparisonArrow.lean:147`, is the more general form:
it takes an arbitrary section `y` of the kernel ideal over `Y` together with a proof that its
value is the restriction of the value of `x`, and states the identity for that `y`.  This one is
the special case `y = ⟨(A.obj.map f).hom x, _⟩`, with the restriction map taken on
`conormalSheaf` rather than on `(conormalSequence ...).X₁`; stated this way it rewrites directly
in the descent computations below. -/
lemma conormalClass_map_restriction {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (x : kernelIdeal φ.hom X) :
    conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J R A B a φ Y
        ⟨(A.obj.map f).hom x, map_kernel φ.hom f x.2⟩ =
      (conormalSheaf.{v, u, w, z} J A B φ).val.map f
        (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J R A B a φ X x) := by
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (toAssociatedModule_map.{v, u, w, z} J A B φ (conormalPresheaf φ.hom) f
    ((kernelIdeal φ.hom X).toCotangent x))
  exact congrArg (toAssociatedModule.{v, u, w, z} J A B φ (conormalPresheaf φ.hom) Y)
    (conormalPresheaf_map_toCotangent φ.hom f x).symm

end ConormalClassAlgebra

/-- Restricting `ξ` of the conormal class of a local section of `ℐ'` is `ξ` of the conormal class
of its restriction. -/
private lemma restrict_apply_conormalClass {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) [HasWeakSheafify J CommRingCat.{w}]
    [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
    [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
    [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
    {A₁ A₂ B : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}} (u : A₁ ⟶ A₂) (E : Functor Cᵒᵖ (Type w))
    (a₂ : A₂ ⟶ B) (e : E ⟶ underlyingPresheaf J B)
    [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom]
    (G : SheafOfModules.{max w u v z} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf B))
    (ξ : conormalSheaf.{v, u, w, z} J (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
      (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) ⟶ G) {Y V : Cᵒᵖ} (i : Y ⟶ V)
    (h : restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e Y) :
    G.val.presheaf.map i ((ξ.val.app Y)
      (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) Y h)) =
    (ξ.val.app V) (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
      (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) V
      ⟨_, map_kernel (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom i h.2⟩) :=
  (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply ξ.val i _).symm.trans <| congrArg (ξ.val.app V)
    (conormalClass_map_restriction.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
      (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) i h).symm

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
  [HasWeakSheafify J CommRingCat.{w}] [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  {A₁ A₂ B : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}} (u : A₁ ⟶ A₂) (E : Functor Cᵒᵖ (Type w))
  (a₂ : A₂ ⟶ B) (e : E ⟶ underlyingPresheaf J B)
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom]
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom]

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom]
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom] in
/-- **The restricted presentation is base change followed by the base presentation**, on
sections. -/
lemma restrictedPresentation_app_apply (X : Cᵒᵖ) (h : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj X) :
    (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom.app X h =
      (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom.app X ((baseChange J u E).hom.app X h) := by
  rw [← hom_of_comp_eq (baseChange_comp_desc J u E a₂ e)]
  rfl

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom]
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom] in
/-- A local lift along the base change morphism of a local section of `ℐ` lies in `ℐ'`: the
ideal `ℐ'` is the preimage of `ℐ`, because the restricted presentation factors through the base
one. -/
lemma mem_restrictedPresentationIdeal_of_baseChange_eq {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (i : U ⟶ V)
    (g : basePresentationIdeal J E a₂ e U) (h : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj V)
    (hh : (baseChange J u E).hom.app V h = (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E).obj.map i g.1) :
    h ∈ restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e V := by
  show (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom.app V h = 0
  rw [restrictedPresentation_app_apply J u E a₂ e V h, hh, NatTrans.naturality_apply,
    show (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom.app U g.1 = 0 from g.2, map_zero]

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom]
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom] in
/-- A local section of `𝒜₁[ℰ]` killed by base change lies in `ℐ'`. -/
lemma mem_restrictedPresentationIdeal_of_baseChange_eq_zero (X : Cᵒᵖ)
    (h : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj X)
    (hh : (baseChange J u E).hom.app X h = 0) :
    h ∈ restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X := by
  show (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom.app X h = 0
  rw [restrictedPresentation_app_apply J u E a₂ e X h, hh, map_zero]

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}] in
/-- Base change kills the coefficient of a local section of `𝒥 = Ker u`, because base change is
`u` on coefficients. -/
lemma baseChange_coefficient_eq_zero (X : Cᵒᵖ) (j : A₁.obj.obj X)
    (hj : (u.hom.app X).hom j = 0) :
    (baseChange J u E).hom.app X ((freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E).hom.app X j) = 0 := by
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun k : A₁.obj ⟶ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E).obj ↦ (k.app X).hom j)
    (hom_of_comp_eq (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap_comp_baseChange J u E))) ?_
  show ((freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₂ E).hom.app X).hom ((u.hom.app X).hom j) = 0
  rw [hj, map_zero]

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom]
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom] in
/-- **The ideal `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]` is contained in `ℐ'`.** Base change kills a coefficient in `𝒥` and
the restricted presentation factors through base change, so each generator of `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]` is
killed by the restricted presentation; being an ideal, `ℐ'` then contains the whole of it. This
is what makes the generators of `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]` have conormal classes at all. -/
lemma coefficientKernelIdeal_le_restrictedPresentationIdeal (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    coefficientKernelIdeal J u E X ≤ restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X := by
  rw [coefficientKernelIdeal, Ideal.span_le]
  rintro x ⟨j, hj, rfl⟩
  exact mem_restrictedPresentationIdeal_of_baseChange_eq_zero J u E a₂ e X _
    (baseChange_coefficient_eq_zero J u E X j (RingHom.mem_ker.mp hj))

/-- Membership in the image sieve of the underlying morphism of presheaves of abelian groups of
a morphism of presheaves of modules, read on module sections. -/
private lemma imageSieve_toPresheaf_map_iff {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{t}}
    {M N : PresheafOfModules.{t'} R} (f : M ⟶ N) {U : C} (s : N.obj (op U)) {V : C}
    (i : V ⟶ U) :
    Presheaf.imageSieve ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R).map f) s i ↔
      ∃ x : M.obj (op V), f.app (op V) x = N.map i.op s :=
  Iff.rfl

omit [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}] in
/-- The conormal class of a local section of `ℐ` is, locally on the site, the image under the
conormal map of the conormal class of a local section of `ℐ'`. -/
lemma imageSieve_presentationConormalMap_conormalClass_mem
    [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J u.hom] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective CommRingCat.{w}]
    (U : C) (g : basePresentationIdeal J E a₂ e (op U)) :
    Presheaf.imageSieve ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map
        (presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e).val)
      (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) B
        (u ≫ freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₂ E) (basePresentation J E a₂ e) (op U) g) ∈
      J U := by
  refine J.superset_covering ?_
    (Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J (baseChange J u E).hom (U := op U) g.1)
  intro V i hi
  obtain ⟨h, hh⟩ := hi
  refine ⟨conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
    (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) (op V)
    ⟨h, mem_restrictedPresentationIdeal_of_baseChange_eq J u E a₂ e i.op g h hh⟩, ?_⟩
  exact (presentationConormalMap_conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e (op V) _).trans
    ((congrArg _ (Subtype.ext hh)).trans (conormalClass_map_restriction.{v, u, w, z} J A₁
      (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) B (u ≫ freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₂ E)
      (basePresentation J E a₂ e) i.op g))

/-- **The conormal map of a base change of presentations is surjective.** If `u : 𝒜₁ ⟶ 𝒜₂` is
locally surjective then `ℐ'/(ℐ')² ⟶ ℐ/ℐ²` is locally surjective, i.e. surjective as a map of
sheaves of `ℬ`-modules. -/
instance isLocallySurjective_presentationConormalMap
    [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J u.hom] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective CommRingCat.{w}] :
    PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective J
      (presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e).val := by
  have hunit : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map
      ((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction.{max w u v z}
        (quotientToRingSheaf J (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) B
          (basePresentation J E a₂ e))).unit.app
        ((liftModules.{v, u, w, z} _).obj
          (conormalPresheaf (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom)))) := by
    rw [PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf_map_sheafificationAdjunction_unit_app]
    exact (GrothendieckTopology.W_toSheafify J _).isLocallySurjective
  constructor
  intro U s
  refine J.transitive (hunit.imageSieve_mem s) _ ?_
  intro V i hi
  rw [Presheaf.pullback_imageSieve]
  obtain ⟨⟨c₀⟩, ht⟩ := (imageSieve_toPresheaf_map_iff
    ((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction.{max w u v z}
      (quotientToRingSheaf J (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) B
        (basePresentation J E a₂ e))).unit.app
      ((liftModules.{v, u, w, z} _).obj
        (conormalPresheaf (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom))) s i).mp hi
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ :=
    (kernelIdeal (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom (op V)).toCotangent_surjective c₀
  have hs : conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) B
        (u ≫ freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₂ E) (basePresentation J E a₂ e) (op V) c =
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf B).obj).obj
        (conormalSheaf.{v, u, w, z} J (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) B
          (basePresentation J E a₂ e)).val).map i.op s := ht
  rw [← hs]
  exact imageSieve_presentationConormalMap_conormalClass_mem.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e V c

/-- A faithful functor reflects epimorphisms. -/
private lemma reflectsEpimorphisms_of_faithful {D : Type*} [Category D] {D' : Type*}
    [Category D'] (F : D ⥤ D') [F.Faithful] : F.ReflectsEpimorphisms where
  reflects {X Y} f hf :=
    ⟨fun {Z} g₁ g₂ hg ↦ F.map_injective (by
      rw [← cancel_epi (F.map f), ← F.map_comp, ← F.map_comp, hg])⟩

/-- **The conormal map of a base change of presentations is an epimorphism** of sheaves of
`ℬ`-modules, as soon as `u : 𝒜₁ ⟶ 𝒜₂` is locally surjective. -/
instance epi_presentationConormalMap
    [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J u.hom] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective CommRingCat.{w}]
    [J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z})] :
    Epi (presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e) := by
  have h₁ : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective
      ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf B)).map
        (presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e)) :=
    isLocallySurjective_presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e
  have := reflectsEpimorphisms_of_faithful
    (SheafOfModules.toSheaf (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf B))
  exact (SheafOfModules.toSheaf (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf B)).epi_of_epi_map
    inferInstance

/-! ### The kernel of the conormal map -/

omit [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}] in
/-- The conormal class of a local section of `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]`, where `𝒥 = Ker u`, is killed by the
conormal map: base change sends a coefficient in `Ker u` to zero, so it sends such a section to
zero. This is the inclusion `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ] ⊆ Ker(ℐ'/(ℐ')² ⟶ ℐ/ℐ²)` of Step 1 of the source's
proof. -/
lemma presentationConormalMap_conormalClass_coefficient_mul (X : Cᵒᵖ) (j : A₁.obj.obj X)
    (hj : (u.hom.app X).hom j = 0) (q : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj X)
    (hmem : (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E).hom.app X j * q ∈
      restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X) :
    (presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e).val.app X
      (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) X
        ⟨_, hmem⟩) = 0 := by
  have hzero : (baseChange J u E).hom.app X
      ((freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E).hom.app X j * q) = 0 := by
    rw [map_mul, baseChange_coefficient_eq_zero J u E X j hj, zero_mul]
  refine (presentationConormalMap_conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e X _).trans ?_
  exact conormalClass_eq_zero.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) B
    (u ≫ freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₂ E) (basePresentation J E a₂ e) X _ hzero

/-- **Uniqueness of the descent along the conormal map.** A homomorphism out of `ℐ'/(ℐ')²`
descends along `ℐ'/(ℐ')² ⟶ ℐ/ℐ²` in at most one way, because that map is an epimorphism. This
is the uniqueness half of the descent Step 1 of the proof of [Stacks 08U8] performs; the
existence half additionally needs the vanishing of the descended map on the kernel. -/
theorem descend_unique
    [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J u.hom] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective CommRingCat.{w}]
    [J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z})]
    (G : SheafOfModules.{max w u v z} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf B))
    (ξ₁ ξ₂ : conormalSheaf.{v, u, w, z} J (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) B
      (basePresentation J E a₂ e) ⟶ G)
    (hξ : presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e ≫ ξ₁ =
      presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e ≫ ξ₂) :
    ξ₁ = ξ₂ :=
  (cancel_epi (presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e)).mp hξ

/-! ### The vanishing hypothesis of the descent -/

section Descend

variable [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J u.hom] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective CommRingCat.{w}]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z})]
  (G : SheafOfModules.{max w u v z} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf B))
  (ξ : conormalSheaf.{v, u, w, z} J (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
    (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) ⟶ G)

/-- The hypothesis of the descent of Step 1 of the proof of [Stacks 08U8], in the form in which
the source states it: the homomorphism out of `ℐ'/(ℐ')²` kills the conormal class of every
generator `j·q` of the ideal `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]`, where `𝒥 = Ker u`. -/
def KillsCoefficientKernel : Prop :=
  ∀ (X : Cᵒᵖ) (j : A₁.obj.obj X), (u.hom.app X).hom j = 0 →
    ∀ (q : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj X)
      (hmem : (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E).hom.app X j * q ∈
        restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X),
      (ξ.val.app X) (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) X
        ⟨_, hmem⟩) = 0

omit [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J u.hom] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective CommRingCat.{w}]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z})]
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom] in
/-- **A homomorphism killing the conormal classes of the generators of `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]` kills the
conormal class of every local section of that ideal.** The induction over the span needs only
the additivity and the semilinearity of the conormal class, since `j·q·r` is again a generator;
and every local section of `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]` does have a conormal class, by
`Stacks.Sites.Conormal.coefficientKernelIdeal_le_restrictedPresentationIdeal`. -/
lemma eq_zero_of_mem_coefficientKernelIdeal (hξ : KillsCoefficientKernel J u E a₂ e G ξ)
    (X : Cᵒᵖ) (x : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj X)
    (hx : x ∈ coefficientKernelIdeal J u E X)
    (hx' : x ∈ restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X) :
    (ξ.val.app X) (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
      (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) X
      ⟨x, hx'⟩) = 0 := by
  replace hx : x ∈ Ideal.span (((freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E).hom.app X).hom ''
    (RingHom.ker (u.hom.app X).hom : Set (A₁.obj.obj X))) := hx
  revert hx'
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    obtain ⟨j, hj, rfl⟩ := hy
    intro hx'
    have hmem : (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E).hom.app X j * 1 ∈
        restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X := by
      rwa [mul_one]
    refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun y : restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X ↦
        (ξ.val.app X) (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
          (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) X y))
      (Subtype.ext (mul_one _) :
        (⟨_, hmem⟩ : restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X) = ⟨_, hx'⟩)).symm ?_
    exact hξ X j (RingHom.mem_ker.mp hj) 1 hmem
  | zero =>
    intro hx'
    exact Eq.trans (congrArg (fun t ↦ (ξ.val.app X) t)
      (conormalClass_eq_zero.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) X
        ⟨(0 : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj X), hx'⟩ rfl)) (map_zero _)
  | add y y' hy hy' ihy ihy' =>
    intro hx'
    have hy₁ : y ∈ restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X :=
      coefficientKernelIdeal_le_restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X hy
    have hy₂ : y' ∈ restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X :=
      coefficientKernelIdeal_le_restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X hy'
    have h1 := (congrArg (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) X)
      (Subtype.ext rfl : (⟨y + y', hx'⟩ : restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X) =
        ⟨y, hy₁⟩ + ⟨y', hy₂⟩)).trans
      (conormalClass_add J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) X
        ⟨y, hy₁⟩ ⟨y', hy₂⟩)
    refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun t ↦ (ξ.val.app X) t) h1) ?_
    refine Eq.trans (map_add _ _ _) ?_
    rw [ihy hy₁, ihy' hy₂, add_zero]
  | smul r y hy ihy =>
    intro hx'
    have hy₁ : y ∈ restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X :=
      coefficientKernelIdeal_le_restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X hy
    have h1 := (congrArg (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) X)
      (Subtype.ext rfl : (⟨r • y, hx'⟩ : restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X) =
        r • ⟨y, hy₁⟩)).trans
      (conormalClass_smul_quotientToRingSheaf.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) X r
        ⟨y, hy₁⟩)
    refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun t ↦ (ξ.val.app X) t) h1) ?_
    refine Eq.trans (map_smul _ _ _) ?_
    rw [ihy hy₁, smul_zero]

omit [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J u.hom]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z})]
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom] in
/-- **Locally, the conormal class of a local section of `ℐ'` killed by base change is killed by
`ξ`.** Such a section lies, locally on the site, in the ideal `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]`, which is the covering
sieve of `Stacks.Sites.FreeAlgebra.coefficientKernelSieve_mem`, and there
`Stacks.Sites.Conormal.eq_zero_of_mem_coefficientKernelIdeal` applies. -/
lemma moduleVanishingSieve_mem_of_baseChange_eq_zero (hξ : KillsCoefficientKernel J u E a₂ e G ξ)
    (Y : C) (h : restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op Y))
    (hh : (baseChange J u E).hom.app (op Y) h.1 = 0) :
    moduleVanishingSieve G ((ξ.val.app (op Y))
      (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e)
        (op Y) h)) ∈ J Y := by
  refine J.superset_covering ?_ (coefficientKernelSieve_mem J u E Y h.1 hh)
  intro V i hi
  have hmem : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map i.op h.1 ∈
      restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op V) :=
    map_kernel (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom i.op h.2
  show G.val.presheaf.map i.op ((ξ.val.app (op Y)) _) = 0
  rw [restrict_apply_conormalClass J u E a₂ e G ξ i.op h]
  exact eq_zero_of_mem_coefficientKernelIdeal J u E a₂ e G ξ hξ (op V) _ hi hmem

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom] in
/-- **A local section of `ℐ²` is locally the image under base change of a local section of
`(ℐ')²`.** Each of the finitely many factors of a product decomposition of the section lifts
along the locally surjective base change morphism, a lift lies in `ℐ'` automatically because
`ℐ'` is the preimage of `ℐ`, and the lifted product therefore has conormal class zero, being a
local section of `(ℐ')²`. -/
lemma exists_sieve_lift_of_mem_sq (Y : C) (r : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E).obj.obj (op Y))
    (hr : r ∈ basePresentationIdeal J E a₂ e (op Y) ^ 2) :
    ∃ S : Sieve Y, S ∈ J Y ∧ ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (i : V ⟶ Y), S.arrows i →
      ∃ k : restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op V),
        (baseChange J u E).hom.app (op V) k.1 =
            (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E).obj.map i.op r ∧
          conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
            (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e)
            (op V) k = 0 := by
  rw [pow_two] at hr
  refine Submodule.mul_induction_on hr ?_ ?_
  · intro g hg g' hg'
    have hβ := isLocallySurjective_baseChange J u E
    refine ⟨Presheaf.imageSieve (baseChange J u E).hom g ⊓
      Presheaf.imageSieve (baseChange J u E).hom g',
      J.intersection_covering (hβ.imageSieve_mem g) (hβ.imageSieve_mem g'), ?_⟩
    rintro V i ⟨⟨k, hk⟩, ⟨k', hk'⟩⟩
    have hkmem : k ∈ restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op V) :=
      mem_restrictedPresentationIdeal_of_baseChange_eq J u E a₂ e i.op ⟨g, hg⟩ k hk
    have hk'mem : k' ∈ restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op V) :=
      mem_restrictedPresentationIdeal_of_baseChange_eq J u E a₂ e i.op ⟨g', hg'⟩ k' hk'
    refine ⟨⟨k * k', Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ hkmem⟩, ?_, ?_⟩
    · show (baseChange J u E).hom.app (op V) (k * k') = _
      rw [map_mul, hk, hk', ← map_mul]
    · refine conormalClass_eq_zero_of_mem_sq.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e)
        (op V) _ ?_
      rw [pow_two]
      exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul hkmem hk'mem
  · rintro x y ⟨S, hS, hx⟩ ⟨T, hT, hy⟩
    refine ⟨S ⊓ T, J.intersection_covering hS hT, ?_⟩
    rintro V i ⟨hiS, hiT⟩
    obtain ⟨k, hk, hk0⟩ := hx i hiS
    obtain ⟨k', hk', hk'0⟩ := hy i hiT
    refine ⟨k + k', ?_, ?_⟩
    · show (baseChange J u E).hom.app (op V) (k.1 + k'.1) = _
      rw [map_add, hk, hk', ← map_add]
    · refine Eq.trans (conormalClass_add J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) (op V)
        k k') ?_
      rw [hk0, hk'0, add_zero]

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z})]
  [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom] in
/-- **Locally, the conormal class of a local section of `ℐ'` whose base change lies in `ℐ²` is
killed by `ξ`.** Subtract from the section a local lift of a product decomposition of its base
change: the lift has conormal class zero and the difference is killed by base change, where
`Stacks.Sites.Conormal.moduleVanishingSieve_mem_of_baseChange_eq_zero` applies. -/
lemma moduleVanishingSieve_mem_of_baseChange_mem_sq (hξ : KillsCoefficientKernel J u E a₂ e G ξ)
    (Y : C) (h : restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op Y))
    (hh : (baseChange J u E).hom.app (op Y) h.1 ∈
      basePresentationIdeal J E a₂ e (op Y) ^ 2) :
    moduleVanishingSieve G ((ξ.val.app (op Y))
      (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e)
        (op Y) h)) ∈ J Y := by
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hlift⟩ := exists_sieve_lift_of_mem_sq.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e Y _ hh
  refine moduleVanishingSieve_mem_of_restrict _ S hS (fun V i hi ↦ ?_)
  obtain ⟨k, hk, hk0⟩ := hlift i hi
  have hmem : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map i.op h.1 ∈
      restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op V) :=
    map_kernel (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom i.op h.2
  have hd : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map i.op h.1 - k.1 ∈
      restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op V) :=
    Ideal.sub_mem _ hmem k.2
  have hbd : (baseChange J u E).hom.app (op V)
      ((freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map i.op h.1 - k.1) = 0 := by
    rw [map_sub, hk, NatTrans.naturality_apply (baseChange J u E).hom i.op h.1, sub_self]
  have hsum := (congrArg (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
      (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) (op V))
    (Subtype.ext (show ((freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map i.op h.1 :
          (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj (op V)) =
        ((freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map i.op h.1 - k.1) + k.1 by ring) :
      (⟨(freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map i.op h.1, hmem⟩ :
        restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op V)) = ⟨_, hd⟩ + k)).trans
    (conormalClass_add J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
      (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) (op V)
      ⟨_, hd⟩ k)
  have hsum2 : conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) (op V)
        ⟨(freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map i.op h.1, hmem⟩ =
      conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) (op V)
        ⟨_, hd⟩ := by
    rw [hsum, hk0, add_zero]
  have heq : G.val.presheaf.map i.op ((ξ.val.app (op Y))
        (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
          (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e)
          (op Y) h)) =
      (ξ.val.app (op V)) (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) (op V)
        ⟨_, hd⟩) := by
    exact (restrict_apply_conormalClass J u E a₂ e G ξ i.op h).trans
      (congrArg (fun t ↦ (ξ.val.app (op V)) t) hsum2)
  rw [heq]
  exact moduleVanishingSieve_mem_of_baseChange_eq_zero.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e G ξ hξ V ⟨_, hd⟩ hbd

/-- **The vanishing of `ξ` on the kernel of the conormal map.** A local section of `ℐ'/(ℐ')²`
killed by the conormal map `ℐ'/(ℐ')² ⟶ ℐ/ℐ²` is killed by every `ξ` killing the conormal classes
of the generators of `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]`.

This is the computation Step 1 of the proof of [Stacks 08U8] performs. The section comes, on a
covering sieve, from a local section `c` of `ℐ'`; its image under the conormal map is then the
conormal class of `β c`, which vanishes, so `β c` lies locally in `ℐ²`, and
`Stacks.Sites.Conormal.moduleVanishingSieve_mem_of_baseChange_mem_sq` finishes. -/
lemma eq_zero_of_presentationConormalMap_eq_zero (hξ : KillsCoefficientKernel J u E a₂ e G ξ)
    (X : Cᵒᵖ)
    (s : (conormalSheaf.{v, u, w, z} J (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
      (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e)).val.obj X)
    (hs : (presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e).val.app X s = 0) :
    (ξ.val.app X) s = 0 := by
  have hunit : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map
      ((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction.{max w u v z}
        (quotientToRingSheaf J (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
          (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e))).unit.app
        ((liftModules.{v, u, w, z} _).obj
          (conormalPresheaf (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom)))) := by
    rw [PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf_map_sheafificationAdjunction_unit_app]
    exact (GrothendieckTopology.W_toSheafify J _).isLocallySurjective
  have hinj : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map
      ((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction.{max w u v z}
        (quotientToRingSheaf J (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) B
          (basePresentation J E a₂ e))).unit.app
        ((liftModules.{v, u, w, z} _).obj
          (conormalPresheaf (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom)))) := by
    rw [PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf_map_sheafificationAdjunction_unit_app]
    exact (GrothendieckTopology.W_toSheafify J _).isLocallyInjective
  refine eq_zero_of_moduleVanishingSieve_mem ((ξ.val.app X) s) ?_
  refine moduleVanishingSieve_mem_of_restrict _ _ (hunit.imageSieve_mem s) (fun V i hi ↦ ?_)
  obtain ⟨⟨c₀⟩, ht⟩ := (imageSieve_toPresheaf_map_iff
    ((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction.{max w u v z}
      (quotientToRingSheaf J (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e))).unit.app
      ((liftModules.{v, u, w, z} _).obj
        (conormalPresheaf (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom))) s i).mp hi
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ :=
    (kernelIdeal (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom (op V)).toCotangent_surjective c₀
  have hsc : conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) (op V) c =
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf B).obj).obj
        (conormalSheaf.{v, u, w, z} J (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
          (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e)).val).map i.op s := ht
  have heq : G.val.presheaf.map i.op ((ξ.val.app X) s) =
      (ξ.val.app (op V)) (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e)
        (op V) c) := by
    refine Eq.trans (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply ξ.val i.op s).symm ?_
    exact congrArg (fun t ↦ (ξ.val.app (op V)) t) hsc.symm
  rw [heq]
  have hbase : conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) B
      (u ≫ freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₂ E) (basePresentation J E a₂ e) (op V)
      ⟨(baseChange J u E).hom.app (op V) c.1,
        baseChange_mem_basePresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op V) c⟩ = 0 := by
    refine Eq.trans (presentationConormalMap_conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e
      (op V) c).symm ?_
    refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun t ↦
      ((presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e).val.app (op V)) t) hsc) ?_
    refine Eq.trans (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply
      (presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e).val i.op s) ?_
    rw [hs]
    exact map_zero _
  refine moduleVanishingSieve_mem_of_restrict _ _ (hinj.equalizerSieve_mem
    (ULift.up ((kernelIdeal (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom (op V)).toCotangent
      ⟨(baseChange J u E).hom.app (op V) c.1,
        baseChange_mem_basePresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op V) c⟩)) 0
    (hbase.trans (map_zero _).symm)) (fun W j hj ↦ ?_)
  have hjd' : (conormalPresheaf (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom).map j.op
      ((kernelIdeal (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom (op V)).toCotangent
        ⟨(baseChange J u E).hom.app (op V) c.1,
          baseChange_mem_basePresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op V) c⟩) = 0 :=
    congrArg ULift.down (hj.trans (map_zero _))
  have hsq : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E).obj.map j.op
      ((baseChange J u E).hom.app (op V) c.1) ∈
      basePresentationIdeal J E a₂ e (op W) ^ 2 :=
    (Ideal.toCotangent_eq_zero _ _).mp
      ((conormalPresheaf_map_toCotangent (basePresentation J E a₂ e).hom j.op
        ⟨(baseChange J u E).hom.app (op V) c.1,
          baseChange_mem_basePresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op V) c⟩).symm.trans hjd')
  have hcmem : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map j.op c.1 ∈
      restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e (op W) :=
    map_kernel (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e).hom j.op c.2
  have hbc : (baseChange J u E).hom.app (op W)
      ((freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.map j.op c.1) ∈
      basePresentationIdeal J E a₂ e (op W) ^ 2 := by
    rwa [NatTrans.naturality_apply (baseChange J u E).hom j.op c.1]
  have heq2 : G.val.presheaf.map j.op ((ξ.val.app (op V))
        (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
          (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e)
          (op V) c)) =
      (ξ.val.app (op W)) (conormalClass.{v, u, w, z} J A₁ (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E) B
        (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E) (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) (op W)
        ⟨_, hcmem⟩) := by
    exact restrict_apply_conormalClass J u E a₂ e G ξ j.op c
  rw [heq2]
  exact moduleVanishingSieve_mem_of_baseChange_mem_sq.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e G ξ hξ W
    ⟨_, hcmem⟩ hbc

/-- **The descent of Step 1 of the proof of [Stacks 08U8].** A homomorphism `ξ : ℐ'/(ℐ')² ⟶ 𝒢`
which kills the conormal classes of the generators of `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]`, where `𝒥 = Ker u`, factors
through the conormal map `ℐ'/(ℐ')² ⟶ ℐ/ℐ²` in exactly one way. Existence is
`Stacks.Sites.Conormal.eq_zero_of_presentationConormalMap_eq_zero` fed to
`Stacks.Sites.Conormal.existsUnique_descend`; uniqueness is
`Stacks.Sites.Conormal.descend_unique`. -/
theorem existsUnique_descend_presentationConormalMap
    [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
    (hξ : KillsCoefficientKernel J u E a₂ e G ξ) :
    ∃! ψ : conormalSheaf.{v, u, w, z} J (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) B
      (basePresentation J E a₂ e) ⟶ G,
      presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e ≫ ψ = ξ :=
  existsUnique_descend (presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e) ξ
    (eq_zero_of_presentationConormalMap_eq_zero.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e G ξ hξ)

/-- **The descent of the difference cocycle of two restriction data.** This is the map `ξ` of
Step 1 of the proof of [Stacks 08U8]: two restriction data for the presentation
`𝒜₁[ℰ] ⟶ ℬ` with the larger coefficient sheaf which *agree on* `𝒥·𝒜₁[ℰ]` have a difference
cocycle `ℐ'/(ℐ')² ⟶ 𝒢` that factors through `ℐ/ℐ² ⟶ 𝒢`, in exactly one way; and `ℐ/ℐ²` is the
conormal term of `NL(α)`, which is the group the source's obstruction class lives in.

The hypothesis is the source's assertion that the two algebra maps of its Step 1 agree on
`𝒥·𝒪_{B'₁}[ℰ]`, and the conclusion is the statement whose absence the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.ConormalIdealRestriction` record. -/
theorem existsUnique_descend_conormalDifference
    [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max w u v z}]
    (ρ σ : IdealRestriction (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) G)
    (hρσ : ∀ (X : Cᵒᵖ) (x : restrictedPresentationIdeal J u E a₂ e X),
      (x : (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₁ E).obj.obj X) ∈ coefficientKernelIdeal J u E X →
        ρ.app X x = σ.app X x) :
    ∃! ψ : conormalSheaf.{v, u, w, z} J (freeAlgebraSheaf J A₂ E) B
        (basePresentation J E a₂ e) ⟶ G,
      presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e ≫ ψ =
        conormalDifference.{v, u, w, z} (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) G ρ σ := by
  refine existsUnique_descend_presentationConormalMap.{v, u, w, z} J u E a₂ e G _ ?_
  intro X j hj q hmem
  have hcoeffmem : (freeAlgebraSheafCoefficientMap J A₁ E).hom.app X j * q ∈
      coefficientKernelIdeal J u E X :=
    Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨j, RingHom.mem_ker.mpr hj, rfl⟩)
  refine Eq.trans (conormalDifference_toAssociatedModule.{v, u, w, z}
    (restrictedPresentation J u E a₂ e) G ρ σ X ⟨_, hmem⟩) ?_
  rw [hρσ X ⟨_, hmem⟩ hcoeffmem, sub_self]

end Descend

